2026-11-07T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2468) 'StableHLO: run-time i32 arithmetic
 # uuid: 858df197-5c50-5d5f-8e9e-2f3cbe48bc89
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Prediscussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-07T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2468) 'run-time i32 values become i32 tensors on the device instead of a refusal.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2468) 'the StableHLO lowering in guest/pjrt-rd/stablehlo.cpp and its generated test cases.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2468) 'Can an i32 value computed at run time reach the device, instead of being refused because it was not already known when the graph was compiled?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2468) 'Today an i32 value is folded away on the host whenever the compiler already knows it, and refused the moment it is computed at run time: an argument, or anything derived from one. Gather's index arithmetic and dynamic masks need those values on the device, not on the host, and the five graphs the probes run (qwen, dit, sconv and the two Kimodo layers) all touch one.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2468) 'Run the generated cases, including zeros of both signs, infinities, NaN and denormals, against XLA CPU's own output from the Zen 2 desk as the reference, and confirm a case built to fail does fail.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2468) 'StableHLO: run-time i32 arithmetic
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2468) 'Hold run-time i32 values as i32 tensors on the device, and add element-wise kernels under XLA's wrapping semantics: add, subtract, multiply, compare, select, clamp, and convert to and from f32. Lift each refusal that exists only for lack of one of these kernels, case by case, so that every case in the generator is either bit-equal on the GPU or carries a measured reason in XFAIL, with all 11 desk gates kept green throughout.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2468) 'Cases and reference
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2468) 'tools/gen_stablehlo_cases.py exercises the special values a run-time i32 path must survive: zeros of both signs, infinities, NaN and denormals. XLA CPU's own output, taken from the Zen 2 desk, is the bit-equal reference for every case; there is no other oracle in use here.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2468) 'What ships
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2468) '- Run-time i32 values held as i32 tensors on the device, never folded away because they were not known at compile time.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2468) '- Element-wise kernels: add, subtract, multiply, compare, select, clamp, and conversion to and from f32, each under XLA's own wrapping semantics rather than a saturating one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2468) '- Refusals lifted only where one of the kernels above now covers the case; a case no kernel covers keeps its refusal unchanged.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2468) 'Acceptance
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2468) '- Every case in tools/gen_stablehlo_cases.py is bit-equal on the GPU, or carries a measured reason recorded in XFAIL.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2468) '- A case built to fail does fail; a gate that cannot fail proves nothing.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2468  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2468) '- All 11 desk gates still pass after the change lands.
 # tags: rfd:details
